The  file  contains  information  about  each package in a binary
package repository as a list of variable‐value pairs.  The  vari‐
ables  describing  different  packages are separated by one empty
line.  Each line has the format If the  value  consists  of  more
than  one  line,  each line is prefixed with Multi‐line variables
are guaranteed to be in consecutive lines.  The  following  vari‐
ables are used: (required) The date and time when the package was
built.   (required)  A list of categories which this package fits
in, separated by space.  (required) A one‐line description of the
package.  (optional) A list of dewey  patterns  of  packages  the
package  conflicts  with, one per line.  If missing, this package
has no conflicts.  (optional) A list of dewey patterns  of  pack‐
ages  the  package  depends  on,  one per line.  If missing, this
package has no dependencies.  (required) A more detailed descrip‐
tion of the package.  (optional) A checksum type supported by and
checksum separated by space character.  (optional)  The  name  of
the  binary  package  file.   If not given, can be assumed.  (op‐
tional) The size of the binary  package  file,  in  bytes.   (op‐
tional)  A  URL  where  more information about the package can be
found.  (optional) The type of license this package  is  distrib‐
uted under.  If empty or missing, it is OSI‐approved.  (required)
The  architecture  on which the package was compiled.  (required)
The operating system on which the  package  was  compiled.   (re‐
quired)  The version of the operating system on which the package
was compiled.  (optional) Any options selected  to  compile  this
package.  If missing, the package does not support options.  (re‐
quired)  The  name  of  the  package.  (required) The path of the
package directory within pkgsrc.  (required) The version  of  the
package  tools used to create the package.  (optional) The previ‐
ous path of the package directory within pkgsrc  when  a  package
was moved.  (See below for a renamed package.)  (optional) A list
of shared libraries provided by the package, including major ver‐
sion  number,  one  per  line.  If missing, this package does not
provide shared libraries.  (optional) A list of shared  libraries
needed  by  the  package, including major version number, one per
line.  If missing, this  package  does  not  require  shared  li‐
braries.   (required)  The size of the package when installed, in
bytes.  (optional) A list of dewey patterns of previous  packages
this  package  replaces,  one per line.  This is used for package
renaming.  The file can be generated using the option.  For exam‐
